  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Halle de Grimaud is an organic, local grocery (fruit and vegetables, butcher-deli, dairy and cheese, farm eggs, wine cellar) that also caters. On weekends, it turns into an oyster bar with a guinguette vibe, with a tasting terrace available for customers to linger.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Pets are allowed: this is confirmed in black and white among the amenities listed by the official regional tourist office listing (provence-alpes-cotedazur.com), which backs up the impression of a friendly, welcoming place. The establishment is open every day from 8am to 7:30pm according to this same source, which itself notes that hours should be checked directly with the establishment.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the weekend oyster bar gets especially lively — check the busy hours if you'd prefer a calmer atmosphere with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The medieval village of Grimaud and its lanes, as well as the lakeside town of Port Grimaud, are a few minutes away by car to extend the outing.</p>
